<!--BlockML Documentation — author semantic structure on imported A03 pages
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task.A03_02_AuthorPages-->
<task:A03_02_AuthorPages xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:source="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.source"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that authors the semantic structure of imported A03 pages
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A03 authoring task: enrich every page imported by A03_01_CopyData with
    a content scaffold that A04 will render. This task does not copy
    or delete A03 data.

    - **Import** — A03_01_CopyData already wiped A03 data and imported the
      full A02 data tree with packages and names remapped
    - **Identity** — title, purpose, detailLevel, pageType, is stay on
      the imported A03 page
    - **Page semantics** — keep the page-level authoritativeSources,
      scopes, readerOutcomes, learningObjectives, exclusions, and
      supportingPoints from A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons; refine them only
      when the bound sources justify a tighter wording
    - **Content** — author DocPage.content as Sections and ContentElements
      that refine page semantics at element level — each element carries
      subsets of the page's sources and semantic claims
    - **Links** — see / source / Navigation targets may name only A03
      Blocks or lib Blocks from authorativeSources; never a Block from
      another sector
    - **Template** — org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.example.PageExample_A03
      is the structural pattern only, not a domain-content source
    - **Sources** — authorativeSources is BlockMLSourceSet, the same set as
      A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          Author the content scaffold that specifies what each imported
          A03 page must show. Sector 3 writes specification, not the
          finished site. Sector 4 (A04_RenderingSector) renders prose,
          examples, and code from that specification.

          A03_01_CopyData has already wiped live A03 data and imported the
          full A02 data tree with packages and names remapped. This task
          does not copy, delete, or recreate DocSet, Pages, or PageGroups.
          Do not read leftover trees such as data_IGNORE. Do not read
          BmlDocSetPlan as the identity source. Do not invent pages that
          are not in BmlDocSet_A03.pages. Do not edit A02. Do not write
          Pages outside a03.

          Use org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.example.PageExample_A03
          only as a structural template (member shape, content roles,
          how page and element semantics bind to sources). Do not copy
          its domain claims onto other pages.

          Keep the imported page identity (is, isNot, title, purpose,
          detailLevel, pageType, lib see-links). Keep the page-level
          semantic scaffold from A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons:
          authoritativeSources, scopes, readerOutcomes, learningObjectives,
          exclusions, and supportingPoints. Those fields are the starting
          point for structuring content — do not discard and regenerate
          them from scratch. Refine a page-level instance only when the
          bound sources justify tighter wording; do not contradict or
          broaden what A02 already established.

          Discard only DocPage.content. Regenerate content from the kept
          page semantics, purpose, and see links. Keep the FQN / file path
          so the same Block is updated.

          1. Read the imported A03 pages
          Read org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.BmlDocSet_A03.
          Walk BmlDocSet_A03.pages in listed order. For each listed A03
          DocPage, inspect is, isNot, documentation, references/see, title,
          purpose, detailLevel, pageType, authoritativeSources, scopes,
          readerOutcomes, learningObjectives, exclusions, and
          supportingPoints. Identity and page-level semantics stay.
          Also note BmlDocSet_A03.homePage and, on each A03 PageGroup,
          pages and landingPage — this task does not rebuild those slots.

          Resolve the page source set from Page.authoritativeSources
          (AuthorativeSourceSet.includedTypes). Every lib FQN bound at
          page level is the ceiling for this page. Element-level sources
          must be subsets of that set — never introduce a lib Block the
          page set does not already cover.

          2. Open the authoritative sources
          Resolve this task's authorativeSources TypeSelectors (scan type
          for each selector on org.blockml.bml.bml.bmldocs.lib.source.BlockMLSourceSet).
          That set is the same whitelist as A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons:
          org.blockml.bml.constraint.**, org.blockml.bml.core.**,
          org.blockml.bml.definition.**, org.blockml.bml.documentation.**,
          org.blockml.bml.exception.**, org.blockml.bml.group.**,
          org.blockml.bml.language.**, org.blockml.bml.mapping.**,
          org.blockml.bml.meta.**, org.blockml.bml.relation.**,
          org.blockml.bml.service.**, org.blockml.bml.status.**,
          org.blockml.bml.type.**, org.blockml.bml.unit.**,
          org.blockml.bml.validation.**.

          Those lib Blocks are the only non-A03 Blocks an A03 page may
          reference (see, page authoritativeSources, element
          authoritativeSources, annotation sources). Never link a Block
          from another sector (a01, a02, a04, or any later sector). Never
          keep an A02 page or PageGroup FQN on an A03 page.
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.** (for example BlockMLSourceSet and
          lib rules) may also be referenced. Docgen types
          (org.blockml.bml.docgen.**) may appear as structural see-links
          (for example Navigation on an Index page), not as sector content.

          For each candidate source, inspect is, documentation, and
          references — do not guess from the FQN alone.

          3. Author content that refines page semantics at element level
          For each A03 page, start from the imported purpose, title, see
          links, and the kept page-level semantics. The page aggregations
          define what the page must cover overall; content distributes
          and sharpens those claims across Sections and ContentElements.

          Inspect PageExample_A03, then inspect DocPage, Section,
          ContentElement, and org.blockml.bml.docgen.semantic.* for member
          shape. Section carries heading, purpose, and nested content.
          ContentElement carries purpose, message, role, detailLevel,
          weight, and the five semantic aggregations plus
          authoritativeSources (TypeReferenceEntity links to lib Blocks).

          Distribution rule — page semantics → element semantics:
          - Every page-level scope, readerOutcome, learningObjective,
            exclusion, and supportingPoint must be reflected somewhere
            in the content tree — on a Section purpose, a ContentElement
            message, or as owned semantic instances on that element.
          - Split when it helps structure: five page scopes may become
            five elements each carrying one refined Scope instance whose
            summary narrows that page scope to what this element treats.
            One page readerOutcome may split across several Paragraphs;
            several page supportingPoints may merge onto one List.
          - Element semantics are refinements, not copies: summary and
            message state the element-local claim; they must stay within
            the parent page instance they refine. Do not introduce topics,
            outcomes, or sources the page semantics do not already cover.
          - Element authoritativeSources are subsets of the page set:
            TypeReferenceEntity links to lib FQNs already listed in the
            page AuthorativeSourceSet. Pick the Blocks that ground this
            element's claim — not necessarily all page sources on every
            element. Semantic-instance authoritativeSources on elements
            tighten further when a SupportingPoint or Scope names a
            narrower claim.

          Author content as an ordered semantic scaffold:
          - Section (heading + purpose + nested content) for thematic
            groupings aligned with page scopes or learning objectives
          - ContentElements (Paragraph, List, ListItem, CodeBlock,
            Navigation as needed) for the claims within each section
          - on each ContentElement set purpose, message, role
            (org.blockml.bml.docgen.role.*), detailLevel
            (org.blockml.bml.docgen.level.*), and weight
            (org.blockml.bml.docgen.weight.*)
          - attach scopes, readerOutcomes, learningObjectives,
            supportingPoints, and exclusions on ContentElements when they
            sharpen the element's claim; omit an aggregation when the
            element inherits the claim implicitly from its Section purpose
            alone and a duplicate instance would add no precision
          - omit CodeBlock.code — A04 generates the listing from message,
            supportingPoints, exclusions, and authoritativeSources
          - omit finished reader-facing article prose, HTML, and filled
            example bodies; message states the claim to convey, purpose
            states why the element exists for the renderer

          Index / menu pages (pageType Index, for example TableOfContents):
          keep the imported page semantics. Author DocPage.content as a
          Navigation tree whose NavigationItem targets are A03 pages only
          (from BmlDocSet_A03 and the A03 PageGroups). Do not invent
          conceptual body on an Index page. NavigationItem.target and any
          in-page continuation link may name only A03 pages listed on
          BmlDocSet_A03.

          Never list an A02, A01, or A04 Block in see,
          authoritativeSources, annotation sources, or Navigation.

          The result is a page whose kept page-level semantics are
          decomposed into a content tree that specifies exactly which
          ideas, sections, roles, and source subsets A04 must manifest —
          not the manifested page itself.

          4. Export A03 pages from the catalog
          Export each A03 page authored here from
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library if it is not already in the
          catalog. Do not remove catalog entries of other sectors. Do not
          remove PageExample_A03 if it is catalogued.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
  <aggregations>
    <authorativeSources override="true">
      <composition>
        <source:BlockMLSourceSet />
      </composition>
    </authorativeSources>
  </aggregations>
</task:A03_02_AuthorPages>
